Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c95155ef6398ce8145b5954d3ab83ebbcb3a55e63f84dcf2bd1c72475fc11dea","compact":"8de15dc03e75d1b6a5ce4936386182c27adccfe68fd79d05ea80a8576053c179","nasal":"8de15dc03e75d1b6a5ce4936386182c27adccfe68fd79d05ea80a8576053c179"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":7,"english":"In that prime of cities, there was none who had not at his command a plenteous supply of the good things, and there was no householder who was not well off in horses and kine, and corn and wealth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e79f6835634e542f7f9fcae9a78badaa748ed30b287e7add646a86ce9e79621f","compact":"34099c525c9dc0ea9f867152975f077b63e8e3dafda02c4eb31edb4291f039f1","nasal":"11a6e6f1f7699772fe1621fd9eadd00c1c49b28d8e9903d70d08c3a3c4997cc7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":8,"english":"And one could see nowhere in Ayodhyā persons given up to lust, or unsightly, or crooked-minded, or unlettered, or atheistical.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5b4e15335578fd598e992888ba8cb1d13de8ca4e099d9fa1771d1d70646db20a","compact":"320212fd3310147dd526b57222244ff6b90aaf688525905232c3d2d0b73610ba","nasal":"0d020fd4d2cd3e7b9a40a07cc1b93dedc218a2917a5c3a12f0faf5d9d285e68b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":9,"english":"And all the men and all the women were of excellent character, and subdued senses, and a happy frame of mind, and both on respect of occupation and conduct spotless like to the Maharsis.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20e9bef7658f4812384438f78643bdf22759c23059f0b06635b9247d5b00a28b","compact":"b13e230c6259fd8ddecb07ffe9cd26f0810cb1b6889ce7bc0794a833a5801587","nasal":"b13e230c6259fd8ddecb07ffe9cd26f0810cb1b6889ce7bc0794a833a5801587"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":10,"english":"And all wore ear-rings and tiaras and garlands, and abundantly enjoyed the good things of life. And all were clean, daubing their limbs, and perfuming their persons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07cb80e84a8212e7896ae763cf856c46b396ba5ca08db7ae05fd7ce67b008897","compact":"5bbfc14f014c28fe247ab45578154f20b8f29ab2cca847551be9629aa55fa19b","nasal":"b09868e7c95c416e086c7a0092dad7c7d773e6d896e3609fcf71a16e73451c4c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":11,"english":"And feeding on pure food, and giving away, and wearing Angadas (A bracelet worn upon the upper arm) and Niskas (An ornament for the breast or neck.) and hand-ornaments, and repressing passions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6efbdc0b8f706f1be2dbfc5ee7b6e79469e67a93545769277d373706db4b72a2","compact":"4104ccba0521eacc36f2fac8c39683c18769d63ec181dbb86641235aa3a858b6","nasal":"921f8792c02bd5910ab074362b9dc91d1cc9bbd478d88e63a2fad6c6dcd3fdd6"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":12,"english":"There were not on Ayodhyā persons not lighting the sacrificial fire, or not performing sacrifices, or mean-minded, or thieving, or engaged in improper occupations, or of impure descent.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.299,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49550e6a201d9e9b58536336ccc0d98681c4796cd8fe321d3341da6be34919b3","compact":"ea2d06ad85e94c8d9b51a4db7d565fa75fd00f9b5ba996bc5f260e169dc04fc1","nasal":"ea2d06ad85e94c8d9b51a4db7d565fa75fd00f9b5ba996bc5f260e169dc04fc1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":13,"english":"The Brāhmaṇas of subdued senses were always engaged in the performance of their own duties, giving away in charity, and studying, and receiving gifts with discrimination.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"535e68ad0c298f683334a04e9de56ce973a3b446fea951743f7e8e4d53b36dca","compact":"d004809b95eea9b5c74c9e95faa41583991f77f42c88bf687621b3537c188303","nasal":"60b1b9ae9d9551b55257d6cdc48ae8c0599babb92e26e9fcc00e7eeaf7240df9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":14,"english":"None of them was atheistical or untruthful or be reft of hearing scriptures or detracting or incompetent or illiterate.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.783,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1533c05545ef016632372bff838a72a62d4802704f4d8cb7ff4735180a3eff4c","compact":"ee38a2c0e277f90fa34d748d1326a5886f6ecd3d836ed5c348a24723d0968dc8","nasal":"ee38a2c0e277f90fa34d748d1326a5886f6ecd3d836ed5c348a24723d0968dc8"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":15,"english":"There was no Brāhmaṇa who was not versed in the Vedas and Vedangas, or poor-spirit, or of insane mind, or afflicted. And no man and no woman was seen devoid of grace or beauty, or lacking in reverence for their monarch.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.6,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-15","DUTT-1-6-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e8d1e72278d67e917ee63da2d136c98e5a5b565e9e7dde5557cb53b364fcb721","compact":"e0174e3b1ba3ed23b748ca88a001e3d8c863be1d98ca0554fe1f659e590390dd","nasal":"019275d72960c53aa6ddc1f9a9b24cf68bd006c57a6352a03bdc8e5bb0c415b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":16,"english":"The four orders with Brāhmanas at their head contained persons serving gods and guests, and endowed with gratitude, and munificent, and heroic, and possessing prowess. And the men were long-lived; and ever abode by duty and truth; and lived in that best of cities, always surrounded by sons and grandsons and wives.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.348,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-17","DUTT-1-6-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f5c14358ccd240ec427b7a6b7ed74a35c76b64c00b83de6ca4dbe48b591631ed","compact":"8458516a062cfee6307aaad189fa10a21f33e6db35dd80ffabf87ee4c598fd87","nasal":"8458516a062cfee6307aaad189fa10a21f33e6db35dd80ffabf87ee4c598fd87"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":17,"english":"The Kşatriyas were obedient the Brahmanas, and the Vaisyas followed the Kșatriyas, and the sadras, occupied with their proper vocations, ministered to the three other orders.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6139c7bc07397fe7263480000e2e1dccbb902a7871a4f05c2908d6397d05d6f7","compact":"7e3168f253ce795bbc0c2cb5903aff5f54cebeba184fc7e41e66cdd87cc444c1","nasal":"7e3168f253ce795bbc0c2cb5903aff5f54cebeba184fc7e41e66cdd87cc444c1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":18,"english":"That city was ably govered by Dasaratha that lord of Ikşvāku's line, even as that foremost of men, the intelligent Manu, had governed it before him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4a0b4bd29844d61aed9b9d5846ce5852465ade715c0294658ee6632813d00670","compact":"f351198d44fa5b6d1a79f4d844cf8af7143a21451934961f35c7e5cc5b119fc8","nasal":"121f8464318605be25687eaddee3fd1b6d34e4a2d687e5f5e32e4cd701de2762"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-6-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":6,"verse":19,"english":"And as a mountain-cavern abounds with lions, it was filled with warriors resembling flaming fire, of straight ways, unforbearing, and of accomplished learning. to","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-6-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1006019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f6dd9105b49873fd3c4402525a3ae6b52a59bf8bb91db82ce4c1ad0095668892","compact":"304113fb5cf4afb7bc1e469ac8d05d131264439585e25238845744f9714dafd5","nasal":"304113fb5cf4afb7bc1e469ac8d05d131264439585e25238845744f9714